YAMNet (singing detection)
--------------------------
The optional singing detector runs Google's YAMNet audio-event classifier.

  Model:      YAMNet v1, trained on AudioSet (521 classes)
  Copyright:  2022 Google LLC (tensorflow/models, research/audioset/yamnet)
  Licence:    Apache License 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)
  Upstream:   https://www.kaggle.com/models/google/yamnet (tfhub.dev/google/yamnet/1)
              https://github.com/tensorflow/models/tree/master/research/audioset/yamnet

The ONNX file is not part of this repository. `tea-asr model-prepare` downloads
it from https://huggingface.co/audiomagic/yamnet-onnx at the revision pinned in
`models.lock.json` and `src/tea_asr/yamnet.py`. That file is a format
conversion of Google's SavedModel made with tf2onnx (opset 15); per its README
no weights were retrained, fine-tuned, pruned or quantized. The Apache-2.0
LICENSE text ships with it. `yamnet_class_map.csv` is byte-identical to Google's
file at tensorflow/models commit dfffd623b6be8d1d9744b8e261fbac370d17c46d.

The AudioSet ontology and labels are released by Google under CC BY 4.0.

Citations:
  S. Hershey et al., "CNN Architectures for Large-Scale Audio Classification",
  ICASSP 2017.
  J. F. Gemmeke et al., "Audio Set: An ontology and human-labeled dataset for
  audio events", ICASSP 2017.

This project only runs the unmodified weights; the singing decision logic
(src/tea_asr/singing.py) is original to this project.

FunASR CT-Transformer (punctuation restoration)
-----------------------------------------------
The optional punctuation restorer runs FunASR's CT-Transformer Chinese/English
punctuation model.

  Model:      iic/punc_ct-transformer_zh-cn-common-vocab272727-pytorch
              (Alibaba DAMO Academy / Tongyi Lab, FunASR)
  Licence:    Apache License 2.0, as stated on the model's ModelScope card
              https://modelscope.cn/models/iic/punc_ct-transformer_zh-cn-common-vocab272727-pytorch
  Reference:  Chen et al., "Controllable Time-Delay Transformer for Real-Time
              Punctuation Prediction and Disfluency Detection", ICASSP 2020.

The ONNX int8 file is not part of this repository. `tea-asr model-prepare`
downloads sherpa-onnx's conversion
(https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/tag/punctuation-models,
`sherpa-onnx-punct-ct-transformer-zh-en-vocab272727-2024-04-12-int8.tar.bz2`)
and verifies the archive and file SHA-256 values pinned in `models.lock.json`
and `src/tea_asr/punctuation.py`. The sherpa-onnx project (Apache-2.0) did the
conversion and quantization; this project does not use its Python package.
The tokenizer and windowed decoder in src/tea_asr/punctuation.py follow
sherpa-onnx's offline-punctuation-ct-transformer-impl.h and FunASR's
ct_transformer code, reimplemented on onnxruntime. Model and attribution are
retained as the FunASR model license asks.

